Rest API Request Methods
==========================
- GET(To fetch the resource i.e. data/record from db)
- POST(To add a new resource)
- PUT(To add a new resource or update the existing resource)
- DELETE(To delete the existing resource)

GET
==========
M - url(Base_URL+Path+Endpoint)
O- params(query params as a dic), usually in manual request query params in url will be like ?key=value&key=value etc..

Validation
------------
status_code(200)
response json


POST
=========
M- url(Base_URL+Path+Endpoint)
M - json(as a dic or JSON format)
O - headers(token)

Note : No need to pass 'Content-Type' in headers, it will be auto taken


Validation
------------
status_code(201)
response json


PUT
=====
M - url(Base_URL+Path+Endpoint/ID captured from post response)
M - json(as a dic or JSON format, the json will be same as of POST but with updated data)
O - headers(token)

validation
-------------
status_code(200)
response json

Delete
==========
M - url(Base_URL+Path+Endpoint/ID captured from post/put response)
o - params

validation
----------
status_code(204)

Note :
- The important parameters/arguments that I can pass to requests keywords are url, json/data, headers, cookies, auth & timeout(how much time to wait for the server response before giving up, by default it is set to a reasonable time, no need to add it generally).
- The API response will have the following imp components
status_code,json(),headers & cookies

Response objects
=================
response.status_code

response.json() - It will return the parsed response JSON

response.headers & response.cookies both will be in the dic form only, so I can directly use them.

How to check the status
========================
- If the expected_status parameter is used with the requests keywords, then it will be checked there, if it's not used no valiadtion is done at that level.
- status should be  201  response

Json file path
==============
The path can abs path with '/' slahes or it can be relative to project, as for Resourse in settings

